# Modified by Shipwright, 2026: rebranded as Shoal Messages; see CHANGES-FROM-UPSTREAM.md.
# D-Bus activation for a push that arrives while Shoal Messages is not running.
#
# A second activation entry beside org.shipwright.ShoalMessages, and it has to be: SailJail
# grants an application exactly one name, that one is already spent on the share
# activation, and claiming a child of it comes back as ServiceUnknown. The
# org.unifiedpush.Connector.* namespace exists for this and is granted by the
# UnifiedPush permission.
#
# The mode travels in the environment, not in argv. SailJail matches the command
# line it is handed against the desktop file's Exec and ExecDBus templates
# exactly — one extra word is refused with "Command line does not match
# templates" — and it does not inspect the environment. `env` runs outside the
# sandbox and the variable is inherited through it; what sailjail sees after the
# `--` is a bare /usr/bin/shipwright-shoal-messages, which matches the template the icon
# uses. So one desktop file serves the icon, the share and the push alike.
[D-BUS Service]
Name=org.unifiedpush.Connector.ShoalMessages
Exec=/usr/bin/env SHOAL_MESSAGES_PUSH_WAKE=1 /usr/bin/sailjail -p shipwright-shoal-messages.desktop -- /usr/bin/shipwright-shoal-messages
